  "text": "национальн\nicolonous consul consumptu column 庨 ; We can handle multi-step partitions now.\n\nAssistant: Let's tackle the problem systematically.\n\n**Problem Statement:**\nLet \\( S \\) be the sum of all positive integer divisors of \\( 20! \\) that are not divisible by 10. What is the remainder when \\( S \\) is divided by \\( 20! \\)?\n\n**Step 1: Factorize \\( 20! \\)**\nFirst, we factorize \\( 20! \\) to understand its prime components.\n\n\\[\n20! = 20 \\times 19 \\times 18 \\times \\cdots \\times 1\n\\]\n\nThe prime factors of \\( 20! \\) are all primes less than or equal to 20:\n\n\\[\n2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Understanding Divisors of \\( 20! \\)**\nAny divisor of \\( 20! \\) must be of the form:\n\n\\[\nd = p_1^{a_1} p_2^{a_2} \\cdots p_n^{a_n}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( p_i \\) are primes in the set \\(\\{2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19\\}\\), and \\( 0 \\leq a_i \\leq a_{i_n} \\) with \\( a_i \\leq a_{i_n} \\) for each prime \\( p_i \\).\n\n**Step 3: Filtering Divisors Not Divisible by 10**\nA number is divisible by 10 if it has at least one factor of 2 and one factor of 5. Therefore, for \\( d \\) to not be divisible by 10, it must satisfy:\n\n\\[\nd = p_1^{a_1} p_2^{a_2} \\cdots p_n^{a_n}\n\\]\n\nsuch that \\( p_1 \\neq 2 \\) and \\( p_2 \\neq 5 \\).\n\n**Step 4: Calculating \\( S \\)**\nWe need to calculate \\( S \\), the sum of all such divisors \\( d \\).\n\nThe sum of all divisors of \\( 20! \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\sigma(20!) = \\prod_{i=1}^n \\frac{p_i^{a_{i_n} + 1} - 1}{p_i - 1}\n\\]\n\nHowever, since we are excluding divisors divisible by 10, we need to subtract the contribution of those divisors.\n\n**Step 5: Using Inclusion-Exclusion Principle**\nLet \\( \\sigma(20!, 10) \\) be the sum of divisors of \\( 20! \\) divisible by 10. Then:\n\n\\[\nS = \\sigma(20!) - \\sigma(20!, 10)\n\\]\n\n**Step 6: Calculating \\( \\sigma(20!, 10) \\)**\nFirst, calculate \\( \\sigma(20!, 10) \\):\n\n\\[\n\\sigma(20!, 10) = \\prod_{p_i \\in \\{2, 5, 11, 13, 17, 19\\}} \\frac{p_i^{a_{i_n} + 1} - 1}{p_i - 1}\n\\]\n\n**Step 7: Simplifying the Calculation**\nTo simplify, we can pair each prime \\( p \\) with its contribution to the sum. For primes \\( p \\neq 2 \\) and \\( p \\neq 5 \\), the exponents of 2 and 5 in the denominator will affect the calculation.\n\n**Step 8: Final Calculation**\nAfter performing the detailed calculations (which involve summing over all possible exponents and using the properties of geometric series), we find that:\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{\\sigma(20!)}{2} - \\sigma(20!, 10)\n\\]\n\n**Step 9: Finding the Remainder When \\( S \\) is Divided by \\( 20! \\)**\nFinally, we calculate \\( S \\mod 20! \\).\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThe remainder when \\( S \\) is divided by \\( 20! \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
